 ## Hiscores
 - **Boards:** all-time top N (N **(prep)**, e.g. 50), plus daily and weekly boards keyed by UTC period.
-- **Entries:** the player's Roblox display name and user ID, the score and the level reached.
+- **Entries:** the player's Roblox display name and user ID, the score, the level reached and the revives the run used (f0186).
 - **Submission:** only the server submits, from its own simulated result, at game over. Clients never send scores.
 - **Top-10 runs (2026-10-21, d0124):** besides each player's best row on every board, the all-time board keeps one list of the ten best runs of all players, so one player can hold several places (rows: 10 plus one per player). Only all-time has it; today and this week stay one best row per player. Game over shows the run's place on that list, or that it is not in the all-time top 10. The lobby's all-time panel lists those ten runs and ends with the viewer's own best: the one personal-best line, by the user's choice. Rows stored before the list existed start it, one entry each. (R0044)
 - **Storage:** behind a Logic-facing interface. A fake store is used in tests, and Roblox's ordered store in the adapter. Beta and production have separate stores, because they are separate experiences.
@@ -117,7 +117,9 @@ The user's words: "Unless in playtest (it will show the screen and accept contro
 - **one free game per hour** per player, a rolling hour from the start of the latest free game, across servers and rejoins; a free game due is used before a game bought and held (G2, G11).
 - After that a game costs **1 Robux**, bought at START GAME in the lobby and charged on arrival in the game place (a teleport that never arrives costs nothing); a game bought and not used is held for later (G3, G9, G10).
 - When the last life is lost the run may **continue with three new lives** for 1 Robux: CONTINUE? counts down 10 s of real time (held while a purchase screen is open), END GAME ends it at once; the score, the level, the pellets eaten, the picked holes and the extra-life flag are kept; continues are unlimited, and one bought after its offer is held for the next (G4, G5, G7, G9).
-- Every board and the top-10 list show the **lives spent** by a run (every life it lost, continues included) as "♥n" after the level; rows stored before show none (G6).
+- **Revives on the boards (f0186)** (the user, 2026-10-31: "highscores shoudl show how many revives were used"; asked, every board, Pickman's included, shows revives used, instead of the lives a run lost): every board, the top-10 list and the viewer's best line show the revives used by a run (the continues it took, bought or held) as "REVIVES n" after the level, "REVIVES 0" for none; rows stored before f0186 show none. The game over shows the same line under the results. Revives never rank a row.
+- **A free game per game (f0186)** (the user, 2026-10-31: "the free game is one per hour per game"): one free game per hour for Pickman alone, kept in Pickman's own record (the `PaidPlay` store); playing Snake, Invaders or Asteroids never uses it, nor Pickman theirs.
+- **The price shown (f0186)** (the user, 2026-10-31: "it shoudl show 5 robux for each game witha slash through showing it is currently on sale for 1 robux"): wherever Pickman shows the price of a game (the line under START GAME, the test purchase screen) it shows "5 R$" struck through, then "1 R$ SALE"; the charge stays 1 R$. A continue's price stays "1 ROBUX".
 - In test mode (everything but a server configured live with both product ids: Studio and the Beta included) the screens show and take their controls exactly as live and **nothing is charged**: our own test screen says so (G1). A server configured live with a product id missing or bad sells nothing and grants nothing free; free games and held credits still work ("Refuse paid play").
 - A store that cannot be read or written lets the player in: a player the lobby let in on a failed read plays that game free; while the pass map cannot be read every arrival with nothing to pay with plays free ("Let them play free", "Let all of them play"). Any other arrival with nothing to pay with is sent back to the lobby (G10).
 - The keys (G12): Return, KeypadEnter or ButtonA CONTINUE or BUY; Backspace or ButtonB END GAME or CANCEL; touch taps the buttons.
